        "code": {
          "text": "Left wrist examination"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Small, well-circumscribed, fluctuant lump on the dorsum of the left wrist, approximately 1–1.5 cm; non-tender to mildly tender; transilluminates. Overlying skin normal, without erythema or warmth. Full active and passive range of motion; grip equal bilaterally; neurovascularly intact; pulses and capillary refill normal. No other joint swelling."
      }
